:: WitchEndContract [nobr] {"position":"1350,275","size":"100,100"}
/* The "call the type" desk. Reached from WitchInside in two flows:
   (1) the run is still active and the held key matches the run's
   static house -- the player came straight from HuntOutside to make
   the call; (2) a prior contract hunt ended without a call and the
   ghost identity is stashed on the held slot (pending guess) -- the
   player slept it off and came back the next day.

   Khadija's rule -- "one guess per contract" -- is enforced by the
   resolve step: the dropdown selection is read on submit and the
   held contract is consumed either way. If the player wants to come
   back later (don't guess until you know), they can <<Back>> out and
   the contract stays held. The shop's other surfaces (WitchSale /
   WitchContracts / WitchEctoplasm) remain reachable from WitchInside
   in the meantime. */
<<set _activeContractHunt to setup.HuntController.isActive() and setup.WitchContract.hasHeldContract()>>
<<set _pendingGuess to setup.WitchContract.hasPendingGuess()>>
<<if not (_activeContractHunt or _pendingGuess)>>
	@@.mc-thoughts; Nothing to report.@@<br>
	@@.backbtn; [[Back|WitchInside]]@@
<<else>>
	<<set _heldHouse to setup.HuntHouses.byId(setup.WitchContract.heldHouseId())>>
	@@.location; Khadija's desk@@<br>
	@@.notmc-speech; Well? <<= _heldHouse.label>>. What was in there.@@<br>
	@@.mc-speech; I think it was:@@<br>
	<<ghostTypeDropdown>><br>
	<br>
	@@.movebtn; [[Name the ghost|WitchEndContractResolve]]@@<br>
	<br>
	@@.backbtn; [[Not yet -- let me think|WitchInside]]@@
<</if>>

:: WitchEndContractResolve [nobr] {"position":"1350,400","size":"100,100"}
/* Locks the player's guess in, settles the contract, and prints
   Khadija's reaction. Two paths:

     * Active-hunt -- run is still in flight (player walked straight
       from HuntOutside). endHunt(success) routes through the shared
       lifecycle cleanup: pay cash on a correct call, burn the
       contract on a wrong one (WRONG_CALL), and tear down the run
       (sanity/energy caps, wardrobe, modifiers, next-seed roll).
     * Pending-guess -- run already ended without a call (caught,
       sanity, exhaustion, time, fled, abandon). The held slot
       carries the stashed ghost identity; settlePendingGuess pays
       cash + XP on success or burns the contract on a wrong call,
       and clears the held slot. No run teardown is needed -- the
       hunt was torn down at its own endHunt call.

   Reveal staging mirrors HuntIdentifyResolve: Khadija's "give me a
   minute" video plays while the 6s <<timed>> wait runs, then the
   result line + .backbtn fade in via .hunt-reveal (text first, buttons
   one second later). Resolution side effects happen at reveal time
   so the contract stays unsettled if the player navigates away
   during the pause. */
<<set _activeContractHunt to setup.HuntController.isActive() and setup.WitchContract.hasHeldContract()>>
<<set _pendingGuess to setup.WitchContract.hasPendingGuess()>>
<<if not (_activeContractHunt or _pendingGuess)>>
	@@.mc-thoughts; Nothing to report.@@<br>
	@@.backbtn; [[Back|WitchInside]]@@
<<else>>
	<<set _guess to setup.Ghosts.ghostTypeSelected()>>
	<<if _activeContractHunt>>
		<<set _trueName to setup.HuntController.ghostName()>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _trueName to setup.WitchContract.pendingGuessGhost()>>
	<</if>>
	<<set _trueGhost to setup.Ghosts.getByName(_trueName)>>
	<<set _correct to _guess eq _trueName>>
	@@.mc-speech; <<= _guess>>.@@<br>
	<<video "characters/witch/witch-result.mp4" { controls: false, loop: false }>>
	@@.notmc-speech; Let's see. Give me a minute.@@<br>
	<<timed 6s>>
		<<if _activeContractHunt>>
			<<if _correct>>
				<<run setup.HuntController.markSuccess()>>
				<<set _summary to setup.HuntController.endHunt(true)>>
			<<else>>
				<<run setup.HuntController.markFailure(setup.HuntController.FailureReason.WRONG_CALL)>>
				<<set _summary to setup.HuntController.endHunt(false)>>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _summary to setup.WitchContract.settlePendingGuess(_correct)>>
		<</if>>
		<<if _correct>>
			<div class="hunt-reveal hunt-reveal-text">@@.notmc-speech; <<= _trueGhost.name>>. Good. Money on the way.@@<br>
				<br>
				<<if _summary.cashPayout gt 0>>
					<span class="mc-action">+$<<= _summary.cashPayout>></span><br>
				<</if>>
				<span class="mc-thoughts">Money: $<<= setup.Mc.money()>></span><br>
				<span class="mc-action">+<<= _summary.xp>> exp</span></div>
		<<else>>
			<div class="hunt-reveal hunt-reveal-text">@@.notmc-speech; <<= _guess>>? No. It was a <<= _trueGhost.name>>. <<= _trueGhost.evidenceLabels()>>. Contract's spent. Try again with a fresh one.@@<br>
				<br>
				<span class="mc-thoughts">No payout. The contract's spent.</span><br>
				<span class="mc-action">+<<= _summary.xp>> exp</span></div>
		<</if>>
		<div class="hunt-reveal hunt-reveal-buttons">@@.backbtn; [[Back|WitchInside]]@@</div>
		<<done>>
			<<run $(".hunt-reveal-text").addClass("show")>>
		<</done>>
		<<timed 1s>>
			<<run $(".hunt-reveal-buttons").addClass("show")>>
		<</timed>>
	<</timed>>
<</if>>
